---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Simple Interest Calculator – Calculate Interest Online"
  description="Calculate simple interest, total interest, and the final amount based on your principal, interest rate, and investment or loan duration."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="Simple Interest Calculator"
  slug="simple-interest-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'simple interest calculator',
    'simple interest calculator monthly',
    'simple interest calculator india',
    'home loan simple interest calculator',
    'simple interest calculator emi'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- QUICK PRESETS BAR -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 text-xs">
        <span class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mr-1 flex items-center gap-1">
          <span>⚡</span> Quick Examples:
        </span>
        <button type="button" class="btn-si-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="100000" data-r="10" data-t="3" data-u="years">📌 Personal Loan (₹1 Lakh @ 10%, 3 Yrs)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-si-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="50000" data-r="12" data-t="6" data-u="months">📅 Monthly Yield (₹50k @ 12%, 6 Mos)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-si-preset rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:border-blue-500 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-p="500000" data-r="8" data-t="10" data-u="years">📈 Long-Term (₹5 Lakh @ 8%, 10 Yrs)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
        <h2 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🪙</span> Simple Interest Calculator
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
          Calculate simple interest, total interest, and the final amount based on your principal, interest rate, and investment or loan duration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <form id="form-si" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <!-- Principal Amount -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-si-principal" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Principal Amount (₹)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-si-principal" value="100000" step="5000" min="1" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="1,00,000" />
          </div>

          <!-- Annual Interest Rate -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-si-rate" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Annual Interest Rate (% p.a.)</label>
            <input type="number" id="inp-si-rate" value="10" step="0.1" min="0" max="100" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="10" />
          </div>

          <!-- Time Period & Unit -->
          <div>
            <label for="inp-si-time" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Time Duration</label>
            <div class="mt-1.5 flex rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800">
              <input type="number" id="inp-si-time" value="5" step="1" min="1" class="w-full rounded-l-xl border-0 p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 focus:ring-0 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="5" />
              <select id="sel-si-unit" class="rounded-r-xl border-l border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 px-3 text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer">
                <option value="years" selected>Years</option>
                <option value="months">Months</option>
                <option value="days">Days (365/yr)</option>
              </select>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-si" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate Interest →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-si" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">
            Clear (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <p id="err-si" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION (Hidden Initially) -->
      <div id="si-results-section" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-5">
        
        <!-- Main Highlight Card -->
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-emerald-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-emerald-50/40 to-emerald-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/5 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-emerald-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-emerald-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">Total Simple Interest Earned</span>
              <div id="res-si-interest" class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 50,000.00</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Final Maturity Amount:</span>
              <div id="res-si-maturity" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 1,50,000.00</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Principal Deposited</div>
              <div id="res-si-principal" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 1,00,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Interest Rate (p.a.)</div>
              <div id="res-si-rate" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">10%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Time Period</div>
              <div id="res-si-period" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5 Years</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Monthly Interest Yield</div>
              <div id="res-si-monthly" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 833.33</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- HOW THIS INTEREST WAS CALCULATED CARD -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-2">
          <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>🧮</span> How This Interest Was Calculated
          </h3>
          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/80 bg-slate-50/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/60 space-y-1.5 text-xs">
            <div class="font-mono text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400" id="res-si-formula">Formula: Simple Interest = (P × R × T) ÷ 100</div>
            <div class="font-mono font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400" id="res-si-arithmetic">₹1,00,000 × 10 × 5 ÷ 100 = ₹50,000.00</div>
            <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 text-[11px] pt-1 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
              Simple interest accumulates strictly on the initial principal without compounding previous interest earnings.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- INTEREST SCHEDULE (YEARLY & MONTHLY TABS) -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span>📅</span> Interest Schedule
              </h3>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                View yearly or month-by-month simple interest accrual.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
              <!-- View Switcher Tabs -->
              <div class="inline-flex rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-100 p-1 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 text-xs font-bold">
                <button type="button" id="tab-si-yearly" class="active rounded-lg bg-white px-3 py-1 text-slate-900 shadow-xs dark:bg-slate-900 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
                  Yearly Summary
                </button>
                <button type="button" id="tab-si-monthly" class="rounded-lg px-3 py-1 text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-400 dark:hover:text-white cursor-pointer">
                  Monthly Schedule
                </button>
              </div>

              <!-- Download PDF Button -->
              <button type="button" id="btn-si-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download active schedule as PDF">
                <span>📄</span> <span id="txt-btn-si-pdf">Download PDF</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Schedule Table Container -->
          <div class="overflow-x-auto max-h-96 scrollbar-thin">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead id="si-sched-thead" class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold sticky top-0">
                <!-- Injected dynamically -->
              </thead>
              <tbody id="si-sched-tbody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Injected dynamically -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE SLOT (Styled matching age.astro) -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="si-content">
      <h2>How to Use This Simple Interest Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Estimating interest on deposits, bonds, or short-term personal notes is straightforward:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Enter the Principal Amount:</strong> Input your initial deposit or loan principal in Indian Rupees (₹).</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the Annual Interest Rate:</strong> Input the agreed annual interest rate percentage (e.g. 10% per annum).</li>
        <li><strong>Input the Duration:</strong> Enter the numeric time value.</li>
        <li><strong>Select Time Unit:</strong> Choose whether the duration is in <em>Years</em>, <em>Months</em>, or <em>Days</em> (assumes standard 365 days/year).</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate Interest:</strong> Instantly view the total simple interest, maturity value, and monthly interest yield.</li>
        <li><strong>Review the Calculation Breakdown:</strong> Inspect the formula substitution to understand how your figures were computed.</li>
        <li><strong>Explore Schedules:</strong> Toggle between the <em>Yearly Summary</em> and <em>Monthly Schedule</em> to view period-by-period growth.</li>
        <li><strong>Download PDF:</strong> Click <em>Download PDF</em> to save your selected schedule report with official branding.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Simple Interest Calculation Example</h2>
      <p>
        Consider an investment of <strong>₹1,00,000</strong> at an annual simple interest rate of <strong>10%</strong> for a duration of <strong>5 years</strong>:
      </p>
      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-1.5 font-mono">
        <div>Principal (P) = ₹1,00,000</div>
        <div>Annual Rate (R) = 10%</div>
        <div>Time Period (T) = 5 Years</div>
        <div class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 font-bold">Simple Interest = (₹1,00,000 × 10 × 5) ÷ 100 = ₹50,000</div>
        <div class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold">Final Maturity Value = ₹1,00,000 + ₹50,000 = ₹1,50,000</div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Because simple interest only applies to the original deposit, the investor earns a constant <strong>₹10,000 every year</strong> (or ~₹833.33 every month) without any compounding effect.
      </p>

      <h2>Simple Interest vs Compound Interest</h2>
      <p>
        The key difference between simple and compound interest lies in how interest is accrued over multiple periods:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Factor</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Simple Interest</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Compound Interest</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Interest Calculation Base</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Calculated strictly on the initial principal</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Calculated on principal plus accumulated interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Interest on Previous Interest</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">No (zero compounding)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Yes (exponential compounding)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Growth Over Time</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Linear progression (constant periodic yield)</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Exponential progression (accelerates over time)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Common Financial Uses</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Short-term notes, auto loans, simple bonds</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Fixed deposits, mutual funds, savings accounts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Calculation Complexity</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Straightforward arithmetic: <code>P × R × T ÷ 100</code></td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Exponential formula: <code>P × (1 + r/n)^(nt)</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>How Monthly Simple Interest Is Calculated</h2>
      <p>
        When interest is specified on an annual percentage rate (% p.a.) but the tenure is in months, the duration is converted to a fraction of a year:
      </p>
      <p>
        For instance, a loan of <strong>₹1,00,000</strong> at <strong>12% annual interest</strong> for <strong>6 months</strong> yields:
      </p>
      <div class="my-3 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono space-y-1">
        <div>Monthly Interest Rate = 12% ÷ 12 = 1.0% per month</div>
        <div>Total Interest for 6 Months = ₹1,00,000 × 12 × 6 ÷ 1200 = <strong>₹6,000</strong></div>
        <div>Total Repayment Amount = ₹1,00,000 + ₹6,000 = <strong>₹1,06,000</strong></div>
      </div>

      <h2>Can a Home Loan Use Simple Interest?</h2>
      <p>
        A frequent question from home buyers is whether home loans operate on simple interest. In reality, commercial mortgages and home loans in India and globally use an <strong>amortizing reducing-balance EMI method</strong> rather than simple interest.
      </p>
      <p>
        In an amortizing loan, each monthly installment (EMI) repays a portion of the principal along with the interest accrued on the remaining outstanding balance. A simple interest calculation may offer a quick rough ballpark, but for precise monthly installments, interest schedules, and prepayment planning, you should use a dedicated <strong>Home Loan EMI Calculator</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Simple Interest vs EMI Calculation</h2>
      <p>
        To understand why simple interest differs from a loan repayment schedule:
      </p>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Factor</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Simple Interest</th>
              <th class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">EMI-Based Loan (Amortized)</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Interest Calculation</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Applied on the initial principal for the full tenure</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Calculated monthly on the outstanding reduced balance</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Principal Repayment</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Usually repaid in a single lump sum at the end</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Repaid gradually with each monthly EMI installment</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Monthly Payment</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Interest only or zero until maturity</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Fixed monthly installment combining principal and interest</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-3 font-semibold border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Outstanding Balance</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Remains constant throughout the loan tenure</td>
              <td class="p-3 border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">Decreases every month after each payment</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Simple Interest Calculator for Indian Investors and Borrowers</h2>
      <p>
        This calculator defaults to Indian Rupee (₹) formatting and standard Indian numbering systems (e.g. <strong>₹1,00,000</strong> for 1 Lakh and <strong>₹10,00,000</strong> for 10 Lakhs). While simple interest is widely used for academic learning and informal lending, bank lending terms often involve processing fees, penal interest, or compounding cycles. Always confirm specific terms with your lender.
      </p>

      <h2>Common Mistakes When Calculating Simple Interest</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Using Incompatible Time Units:</strong> Entering 6 months as <code>T = 6</code> without dividing by 12 multiplies the interest by 6 years instead of half a year.</li>
        <li><strong>Confusing Simple and Compound Interest:</strong> Expecting compounding reinvestment returns from a simple interest calculation.</li>
        <li><strong>Assuming All Bank Loans Use Simple Interest:</strong> Most institutional personal and vehicle loans use reducing-balance compounding.</li>
        <li><strong>Overlooking Processing Fees and Taxes:</strong> Total cost of credit may include upfront administrative charges or GST on interest in commercial facilities.</li>
        <li><strong>Treating Estimates as Final Contracts:</strong> Actual interest accrual depends on exact value dates and bank working day conventions.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Important Assumptions and Information</h2>
      <p>
        Please keep the following mathematical assumptions in mind:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Linear Model:</strong> Calculations assume a constant annual percentage rate without compounding or rate revisions.</li>
        <li><strong>Day-Count Convention:</strong> Daily interest calculations assume a standard 365-day Gregorian calendar year.</li>
        <li><strong>Informational Tool:</strong> This calculator provides mathematical estimates and does not constitute certified legal or financial advisory services.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- FAQ SECTION SLOT (EXACTLY 7 FAQs AS REQUIRED) -->
  <Fragment slot="faq">
    <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
      
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800" open>
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            1. How does a simple interest calculator work?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          A simple interest calculator uses the formula <code>SI = (P × R × T) / 100</code> to determine the exact interest accumulated on your initial principal amount over a given number of years, months, or days without compounding.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            2. What is the formula for simple interest?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          The formula is <code>Simple Interest = (Principal × Annual Rate × Time in Years) / 100</code>. The total maturity value is calculated as <code>Principal + Simple Interest</code>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            3. How do I calculate simple interest for monthly periods?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          When the duration is in months, convert months into years by dividing by 12. The formula becomes: <code>SI = (Principal × Annual Rate × Months) / 1200</code>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            4. What is the difference between simple and compound interest?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Simple interest is calculated strictly on the original principal deposit. Compound interest calculates interest on both the principal and the accumulated interest from previous periods, leading to exponential growth.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            5. Can I use a simple interest calculator for a home loan?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Most home loans use an amortizing reducing-balance EMI method rather than simple interest. While simple interest can provide a rough baseline, you should use our dedicated Home Loan EMI Calculator for accurate monthly payment schedules.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            6. Is simple interest the same as an EMI calculation?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          No. Simple interest calculates interest on the full initial principal across the entire tenure. An EMI loan calculates interest monthly on the outstanding balance, which decreases as principal is repaid every month.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-slate-200 p-4 dark:border-slate-800">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none">
          <h3 class="flex items-center justify-between font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
            7. Can I download my simple interest schedule as a PDF?
            <span class="group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform">▼</span>
          </h3>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Yes! Click the "Download PDF" button in the Interest Schedule section. The PDF dynamically exports only your currently selected schedule view (Yearly Summary or Monthly Schedule) with official AIFreecalculator.com branding.
        </p>
      </details>

    </div>
  </Fragment>
</CalculatorLayout>

